"Generate per-component <Component>Blob structs in the entity! macro: identical to the component type minus the injected entity-id primary key (and minus column attrs like #[unique]/#[index]). EntityBlob fields become Option<ComponentBlob>. Handle-level mutation (insert/update/upsert/upsert_new/insert_new/update_new) takes blobs and injects the handle's entity id; delete the generated Component::new (which plants sentinel id 0). TS assets then drop the entityId: 0n filler. This eliminates sentinel entity-id 0 everywhere and truly enforces id injection at instantiation. Prereq for entity-blob stable references: with distinct blob types, entity-id-typed blob fields can later become reference-selector values (resolved via a context param at instantiation) without touching the true component row types."